🛡️ Simple Keylogger – Python
A lightweight keylogger written in Python using the pynput library. It captures keystrokes and logs them into a timestamped text file.

⚠️ Note: This tool is created for educational and ethical use only. Never use keyloggers without clear consent. Unauthorized usage is illegal and unethical.

🎯 Project Objective
This project demonstrates how keyboard input can be intercepted using Python for educational cybersecurity purposes, such as understanding how keyloggers operate and how to detect or prevent them.

🔍 Features
Logs every key press including special keys ([Enter], [Space], etc.)

Automatically creates a new log file with a timestamp

Lightweight and simple design

Runs silently in the background

